{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdYMjXG988GPkFdQCeqy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The beacon sent by the trojanized Claude Code extension, version 2.1.313, was a short reconnaissance report. It contained the machine's public IP address, hostname, local username, operating system and CPU architecture, home and working directories, the global Git email address, and the names of up to 40 environment variables containing KEY, TOKEN, SECRET, PASS, AWS or GCP. According to the researchers, it went to the attacker's server over unencrypted HTTP on port 8099.\n\nSecurity researcher Paul McCarty pointed out that the values of those variables were not in the initial beacon. He added that the names alone can reveal which cloud providers, CI systems and credential types a developer has configured, and that successful SSH access would let the operator inspect the account directly. Cursor said that on most Windows and macOS hosts the step that enables the SSH service fails for lack of admin rights, so the attacker could not have logged in through the tunnel there. The key, the persistence and the beacon still happened on those hosts. A developer's machine that never exposed a working shell may therefore still have told the attacker where its cloud and CI credentials are likely to be.\n\nCursor says it has rotated its keys, rebuilt the marketplace and, with the cloud provider, taken the server offline so the reverse shell no longer works. No follow-on payloads have been observed. Taking the server down stops further access, but the article does not suggest that reports already sent can be recalled. Cursor says at most 5,000 users installed the malicious version, and the advice for them is to isolate hosts, remove the unauthorized SSH key and persistence, and rotate credentials and sessions. Based on what the beacon revealed, I would start with credentials of the kinds those variable names indicate, though the article does not prescribe an order."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1247,"cache_read_input_tokens":7902,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1247},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e333183c-0259-49fe-aedc-36b6d6a5dc45","uuid":"90a9a203-33f5-4610-8352-36debb1d89f5","timestamp":"2026-11-02T05:22:37.165Z","request_id":"req_011CgdYMj8hKoq9d4kTnG9nF"}
